# Dart standards

- `type` aliases over redundant wrappers. Prefer explicit types on public APIs.
- Models: `freezed` (or equivalent generated DTO from OpenAPI). No hand-written `==` / `copyWith`.
- State: Riverpod (`@riverpod` / `Notifier`). No GetX, Bloc, Provider+GetIt.
- Screens do not call `Dio` or know URL paths — only repositories in `data/`.
- `flutter_secure_storage` for refresh tokens. Not `SharedPreferences`.
- `avoid_print` in production paths; use a logger if needed.
- Generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`) are not edited by hand.
- Comments: why-only, English.
